  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member, I want member profiles to open in SwiftHFR exactly as in the patched legacy beta, so that an account migrated from legacy or refreshed many times still sees profiles. ezzz shipped legacy 4.0.3 build 39 (`8c10791e`, `origin/master`) with `5c0f10db` « Profil : conserver le cookie md_id exigé par le forum (#1349) », after `bb58131d` (build 38, already ported by #1379).\n\n### What the legacy patch says (`5c0f10db`, commit message and diff)\n1. HFR now answers **403** to a profile request **without `md_id`**; `md_id` is set **only at login**.\n2. `LoginService.swift`: the login POST now sends **the fields of the forum's own `login.php` form** (`hash_check`, `pseudo`, `password`, `cat`, `page=1`, `config=hfr.inc`, `p=1`, `sondage=0`, `owntopic=0`, `post`, `referer`, `Valider=Valider`); per the commit, with these fields `login_validation.php` also sets `md_id` (legacy « ne l'avait jamais »).\n3. `MultisManager.updateCookies:` **merges** received cookies into the account's (same name, domain, path replaced; others kept) instead of replacing the list, which dropped `md_id` at each launch refresh.\n4. The profile sends the account's cookies completed by the shared storage.\n5. A 403 **without `md_id`** gets a new error, `reloginRequired`: « remove and re-add the account ».\n\n### SwiftHFR today (dev-swift, read by cloud/orch, to verify)\n- Login (`HFREndpoint+Account.swift:12-21`) still sends the **legacy fields** `pseudo, password, action=send, login=Se connecter`. Our capture `W03` (2026-10-26) shows that login setting `md_id` (HFR-PROTOCOL §6c), which **contradicts** ezzz's finding: either HFR changed since, or the legacy app lost `md_id` elsewhere. **Never guess**: capture today's answer for both field sets.\n- Jar updates merge by name/domain/path (`HFRSession.replaceCookies`, `HFRSession.swift:128-137`), like the patch's fix 3; #1385 compares only `md_user`/`md_passs` and notes « a jar drops `md_id` while a stored copy may still list it expired » (`AccountsModel.swift:478-482`).\n- #1379 sends the account's session to profiles; verified 200 with user1 (`R1363b`) on a fresh login.\n- Risks to check: (a) accounts **imported from legacy** (LOT-067) carry legacy's cookie list, **without `md_id`** → 403 forever; (b) `md_id` expires after 30 days (`W03`) while `md_user`/`md_passs` are refreshed → the session stays valid but profiles 403; (c) the iCloud account sync copy (LOT-173) and its merge.\n\n### Scope\n1. **Capture (Mac, test account only)**: login with the legacy fields and with `login.php`'s fields: which cookies each sets today; a profile request with and without `md_id` (`R1363*` series). Record in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c.\n2. Port what the capture proves: the login field set, `md_id` kept through refreshes, imports and sync; a **relogin-required** state (not a generic error) when the session lacks `md_id` or the forum answers 403 with a full session missing it, with the same user message as legacy.\n3. Tests: a profile request carries `md_id`; a refresh never drops it; an imported legacy account without `md_id` gets the relogin state.\n\n### Acceptance\n- Profiles open for a fresh login, a 30-day-old session and an imported legacy account (after the relogin prompt); `### Ledger` row for the legacy evolution (`origin: legacy-evolution`).\n\nRefs #1349, #1363, #1379. Legacy: `bb58131d`, `5c0f10db` (build 39, `8c10791e`).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
